  "scope": [
    "HAL (classic, handle-based) as delivered by ST: SPI_HandleTypeDef with its Instance (the CMSIS device structure SPI1, stm32n6xx.h) and Init configuration; HAL_StatusTypeDef results; the HAL framework headers and ST's stm32n6xx_hal_conf_template.h configured with the SPI module and the DMA module headers the handle type needs (USE_FULL_ASSERT off, as delivered)",
    "Initialisation and de-initialisation from the handle configuration (master mode, direction, data size, clock polarity/phase, NSS management, baud-rate prescaler, bit order, CRC off; SPI_CR1, SPI_CFG1, SPI_CFG2); blocking transmit, receive and transmit-receive of a buffer with a timeout in ms of the HAL time base HAL_GetTick (SPI_TXDR, SPI_RXDR, SPI_SR, SPI_IFCR, SPI_CR2.TSIZE); the handle state and error code",
    "Out of scope: the MSP hooks (weak, empty as delivered), interrupt and DMA transfers (and HAL_SPI_Abort, which uses the DMA module), slave mode, CRC calculation, TI mode, FIFO threshold tuning beyond the default, the extended API, register callbacks"
  ],
  "system_names": [
    "SPI HAL driver",
    "SPI driver",
    "STM32N6 SPI HAL driver"
